# FinLife Assistant - Design System & Styling Guide

## Overview
This document defines the complete design system for the FinLife Assistant mobile app. All components must adhere to these rules for consistent, accessible, and performant UI.

---

## 1. COLOR PALETTE

### Primary Colors
```
Primary Blue:       #2563EB (action buttons, links, highlights)
Primary Dark:       #1E40AF (button hover/active states)
Primary Light:      #DBEAFE (backgrounds, light fills)

Secondary Purple:   #7C3AED (secondary actions, tags)
Secondary Dark:     #5B21B6 (secondary hover/active)
Secondary Light:    #EDE9FE (secondary backgrounds)
```

### Semantic Colors
```
Success Green:      #10B981 (success messages, approved)
Success Dark:       #047857 (success hover)
Success Light:      #D1FAE5 (success background)

Warning Amber:      #F59E0B (warnings, alerts)
Warning Dark:       #D97706 (warning hover)
Warning Light:      #FEF3C7 (warning background)

Danger Red:         #EF4444 (errors, delete actions)
Danger Dark:        #DC2626 (danger hover)
Danger Light:       #FEE2E2 (danger background)

Info Blue:          #3B82F6 (informational messages)
Info Dark:          #1D4ED8 (info hover)
Info Light:         #EFF6FF (info background)
```

### Neutral Colors
```
Black:              #000000 (text, dark elements)
Neutral Dark:       #1F2937 (primary text)
Neutral Medium:     #6B7280 (secondary text, borders)
Neutral Light:      #D1D5DB (disabled, subtle borders)
Neutral Very Light: #F3F4F6 (dividers)
Gray Bg:            #F9FAFB (card backgrounds, surface)
White:              #FFFFFF (primary background)
```

### Usage Rules
- **Backgrounds:** White (#FFFFFF) or Gray Bg (#F9FAFB)
- **Text:** Neutral Dark (#1F2937) on white, Neutral Medium (#6B7280) for secondary
- **Buttons:** Primary Blue (#2563EB) with white text
- **Borders:** Neutral Light (#D1D5DB) - 1px solid
- **Hover states:** Darken primary color by 15% or use darker semantic variant
- **Active states:** Darken primary color by 25%
- **Disabled:** Neutral Light (#D1D5DB) text on Neutral Very Light (#F3F4F6) background

### Dark Mode (Future)
When implemented, use inverted palette:
- White → #1F2937
- #F9FAFB → #111827
- #1F2937 → #F9FAFB
- Primary colors remain same, adjust opacity for transparency elements

