## 7. ACCESSIBILITY (a11y)

### Touch Targets
```
Minimum:        48x48px (WCAG AAA standard)
Icons + text:   pad to at least 44px height
Spacing:        8px between interactive elements
```

### Color Contrast
```
Text on background:     4.5:1 (normal text), 7:1 (AAA preferred)
Icons on background:    3:1 minimum
Button text:            white on #2563EB achieves 8.3:1 ✓
Disabled text:          #D1D5DB on white = 4.2:1 (acceptable)
```

### Semantic Elements
```
Use <Text> with semantic roles when appropriate
Large touch targets have accessible names
Buttons are announced as buttons (not just text)
Images have alt text (contentDescription on Android)
Colors alone don't convey information (add icons, labels)
Form fields have associated labels
Error messages linked to input with aria-describedby equivalent
```

### Focus Management
```
Tab order:      logical flow (left-to-right, top-to-bottom)
Focus visible:  2px outline, 2px offset (all interactive elements)
Focus trap:     none (users can escape modals with back button)
Keyboard nav:   Tab to next, Shift+Tab to previous, Enter to activate
```

